  "body": "The cookie store spec is currently a bit vague about what happens when a cookiechange event fires in a service worker context.  It seems to imply that the SW will be started in that case, but does not explicitly spec this.  Any events fired that start the SW should also extend ExtendableEvent so that the handler can keep the worker alive with waitUntil().\r\n\r\nThis is probably largely solvable by using:\r\n\r\nhttps://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#fire-functional-event-algorithm\r\n\r\nAnd extending for events fired at the SW:\r\n\r\nhttps://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#extendableevent-interface\r\n\r\nA bit awkward that these should not have the waitUntil in other contexts, though.",
